{"type":"standard","title":"Rick Jackson (businessman)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Rick Jackson (businessman)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q138543331","titles":{"canonical":"Rick_Jackson_(businessman)","normalized":"Rick Jackson (businessman)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Rick Jackson (businessman)</span></span>"},"pageid":82355922,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Rick_Jackson_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Rick_Jackson_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/Rick_Jackson_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":512,"height":682},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377232117","tid":"b6841c51-bb34-11f1-b818-06f0559037a9","timestamp":"2026-09-28T12:04:10Z","description":"American businessman and politician (born 1954)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Jackson_(businessman)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Jackson_(businessman)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Jackson_(businessman)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Rick_Jackson_(businessman)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Jackson_(businessman)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Rick_Jackson_(businessman)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Jackson_(businessman)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Rick_Jackson_(businessman)"}},"extract":"Richard Lee Jackson is an American business executive and politician. He is the founder and CEO of Jackson Healthcare, a healthcare staffing and services company based in Alpharetta, Georgia. He is the Republican nominee in the 2026 Georgia gubernatorial election, after defeating President Trump-endorsed lieutenant governor Burt Jones in a primary runoff.","extract_html":"<p><b>Richard Lee Jackson</b> is an American business executive and politician. He is the founder and CEO of Jackson Healthcare, a healthcare staffing and services company based in Alpharetta, Georgia. He is the Republican nominee in the 2026 Georgia gubernatorial election, after defeating President Trump-endorsed lieutenant governor Burt Jones in a primary runoff.</p>"}